  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-PHL826</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PHL 826 strengthens the Philippines&#x2019; compliance with international labour standards and deepens social dialogue to foster a rights-based and inclusive labour market. It supports the Labour and Employment Plan (LEP) 2023 to 2028, particularly the priority on labour market governance and the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF) 2024&#x2013;2028 on sustainable economic development and decent work priority.
 
The initiative benefits government institutions, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations by enhancing their capacity to implement and monitor international labour standards. It prioritizes the ratification and application of key ILO Conventions, including the Violence and Harassment Convention, 2019 (No. 190), Labour Inspection Convention, 1947 (No. 81), Occupational Safety and Health Convention, 1981 (No. 155), and Labour Relations (Public Service) Convention, 1978 (No. 151). It also advances the Freedom of Association and Protection of the Right to Organise Convention, 1948 (No. 87), through follow-up to the 2023 High-Level Tripartite Mission and implementation of the roadmap on Freedom of Association.
 
The strategy is delivered with tripartite constituents and strategic partners to strengthen national mechanisms for compliance, dialogue and policy coherence, supporting more transparent, accountable and inclusive labour market governance.</narrative>
  </description>
